menu "Zigbee probe"

config PROBE_TOUCHLINK_MASTER_KEY
    string "Touchlink master key, 32 hex characters"
    default ""
    help
        The Touchlink master key, index 4, is used by certified Touchlink
        devices to encrypt the transferred network key. It is not included in
        this SDK. Leave empty to use the SDK defaults, which advertise both the
        certification and master keys and prefer the certification key because
        it has the higher bit.

        When set, the key is installed and only the master key is advertised, so
        there is no ambiguity about which key the two sides selected. This is
        the working configuration for a BILRESA E2490, with the widely published
        ZLL master key set in sdkconfig.defaults.

config PROBE_ROLE_ROUTER
    bool "Join as a router instead of forming a network as coordinator"
    default n
    help
        A coordinator forms its own network and cannot be adopted by a remote
        that is off network. Touchlink from such a remote creates a network and
        pulls the target into it, so the target must be a joinable router.
        Enable this to test Touchlink against a factory reset remote.

config PROBE_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID for log shipping"
    default ""
    help
        Leave empty to disable Wi-Fi and log only over serial -- which the
        Zigbee stack tends to kill a few seconds after boot.

config PROBE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default ""

config PROBE_WIFI_SCAN_ON_BOOT
    bool "Log a Wi-Fi scan at boot"
    default n
    help
        Lists every visible AP with channel and signal, and marks the
        configured SSID. Useful when association fails with NO_AP_FOUND.

config PROBE_WIFI_COUNTRY
    string "Wi-Fi country code"
    default "01"
    help
        Two-letter code, e.g. NL, DE, US. The default "01" is world-safe mode
        and only scans channels 1-11; set your country if your AP sits on
        channel 12 or 13, or it will never be found.

config PROBE_LOG_UDP_TARGET
    string "UDP target for log lines"
    default "255.255.255.255"
    help
        Broadcast by default, so no host address has to be configured.
        Set a specific address if your network blocks broadcast.

config PROBE_LOG_UDP_PORT
    int "UDP port for log lines"
    default 5555

endmenu
